  "description": "Find all starting indices of substrings in 's' that are a concatenation of each word in 'words' exactly once and without any intervening characters.",
  "pseudocode": "1. function findSubstring(s, words) {\n2.   if (!s || !words || words.length === 0) return [];\n3.\n4.   const wordLength = words[0].length;\n5.   const numWords = words.length;\n6.   const totalLength = wordLength * numWords;\n7.   const sLength = s.length;\n8.   const result = [];\n9.\n10.  if (sLength < totalLength) return [];\n11.\n12.  const wordCounts = new Map();\n13.  for (const word of words) {\n14.    wordCounts.set(word, (wordCounts.get(word) || 0) + 1);\n15.  }\n16.\n17.  // Iterate through 's' using 'wordLength' different starting offsets.\n18.  // This is crucial to cover all possible starting positions of concatenated substrings.\n19.  for (let offset = 0; offset < wordLength; offset++) {\n20.    let left = offset;\n21.    let count = 0; // Tracks number of words matched in the current window\n22.    const currentWindowCounts = new Map(); // Frequencies of words in the current window\n23.\n24.    // Slide the window (right pointer advances by wordLength each time)\n25.    for (let right = offset; right <= sLength - wordLength; right += wordLength) {\n26.      const currentWord = s.substring(right, right + wordLength);\n27.\n28.      if (!wordCounts.has(currentWord)) {\n29.        // If the current word is not in 'words', reset the window.\n30.        currentWindowCounts.clear();\n31.        count = 0;\n32.        left = right + wordLength; // Move left pointer past the invalid word\n33.      } else {\n34.        // Add currentWord to the window and update its count.\n35.        currentWindowCounts.set(currentWord, (currentWindowCounts.get(currentWord) || 0) + 1);\n36.        count++;\n37.\n38.        // If currentWord count exceeds its required frequency, shrink window from left.\n39.        while (currentWindowCounts.get(currentWord) > wordCounts.get(currentWord)) {\n40.          const wordToRemove = s.substring(left, left + wordLength);\n41.          currentWindowCounts.set(wordToRemove, currentWindowCounts.get(wordToRemove) - 1);\n42.          count--;\n43.          left += wordLength;\n44.        }\n45.\n46.        // If all words are matched in the current window (its length is totalLength).\n47.        if (count === numWords) {\n48.          result.push(left); // Store the starting index of the valid substring.\n49.\n50.          // To find subsequent matches efficiently, slide the window one word to the right\n51.          // by removing the leftmost word.\n52.          const wordToRemove = s.substring(left, left + wordLength);\n53.          currentWindowCounts.set(wordToRemove, currentWindowCounts.get(wordToRemove) - 1);\n54.          count--;\n55.          left += wordLength;\n56.        }\n57.      }\n58.    }\n59.  }\n60.  return result;\n61. }",
